movement:
Create a transparent PNG sprite sheet of the orange striped fire lizard shown in the reference sheet. Keep the identical turquoise eyes, pointed head horns, cream belly, red flame markings, cheek flames, white claws, long flaming tail and clean cartoon line art.
Layout: exactly SIX columns and FIVE rows, 30 equally sized cells. Same character size and facing RIGHT in every cell, generous transparent padding, consistent foot baseline. No text or grid.
Six successive drawings per row:
1. idle breathing loop, subtle chest movement and blinking, gently waving tail;
2. running loop: right contact, down, pass, left contact, down, pass, opposing arm swing;
3. jump: bend knees, push off, extend, tuck legs, float, apex;
4. fall: apex, descend, extend feet, arms balance, approach ground, toe contact;
5. landing: contact, soft squat, absorb, rise halfway, rise, neutral standing.
Smooth progressive changes and stable head/body proportions. All limbs and tail flame fully contained in each cell. Actual alpha transparent background, no colored background or shadows.
